On Tue, Sep 23, 2014 at 11:42 AM, Pierre Abbat <phma@bezitopo.org> wrote:

>
> I did think of "denxi'u", but "engranaje" is already in jbovlaste.


We can have competing words in jbovlaste.


> I don't
> completely understand the etymology (though it has a cognate in French),
> but
> it looks like a root "gran" with a prefix and a suffix, not a word with
> more than
> one root.
>

Right. it's three morphemes. Lujvo don't necessarily consist of roots only,
many rafsi don't correspond to a root word.
Here I found an etymology of the word
http://etimologias.dechile.net/?engranaje

mu'o mi'e xorxes

